# VHDL NoC Router - 2D Mesh (Wormhole Switching)

A synthesizable VHDL implementation of a 5-port Network-on-Chip (NoC) Router using **Wormhole Switching** and **XY Routing** algorithm. This project demonstrates a simplified 2-router version of a larger 4x4 (16-router) mesh network.

## Project Overview

This project implements a complete NoC router that can be used in a 2D Mesh topology. The current design simulates **two connected routers** (Router ID 9 and Router ID 10) to demonstrate the full functionality of the network in a smaller scale.

### Features
- 5-Port Router (North, South, East, West, Local)
- XY Routing Algorithm
- Wormhole Switching
- Round-Robin Arbiter (per output)
- 5×5 Crossbar Switch
- Synchronous FIFO with configurable depth
- Credit-based flow control
- Fully synthesizable

